Phase 9 execution started 2026-10-11 UTC.
Started from Phase 8 commit b44ab944 on a clean worktree.
Plan and coding-general instructions reviewed; implementation inventory and Java 5.5.1 source audit in progress.

P9-01 — offset transition contract:
- Added the public object-safe `OffsetStore` async boundary, `ReadOffsetType`, typed `OffsetRead::{Found, NotFound}`, and shared per-queue state with atomic update/freeze behavior.
- The shared table keeps lock scopes synchronous and short; it snapshots owned offset values and recovers poisoned locks without panicking. A typed lookup error remains separate from Java's `-1` missing sentinel via `OffsetRead::java_value`.
- Added tests for memory absence, topic snapshots, stale increase-only writes, reset behavior, freeze ordering, reloading, removing a frozen entry, and update/freeze concurrency.
- `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-consumer --lib --locked`: PASS (9 tests). An initial test assertion expected an existing reinserted row to be absent; corrected the assertion order and reran successfully.
- `cargo fmt --all` completed; formatting check and complete workspace lint/test gates remain scheduled for phase closeout.
